-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:ff8dbb92e7a55d2ef54c30b1cd6e1d893c252cf1802ef8922cbd5e326bf2acc0","file":"preprints/A-Gepner-stability-condition-on-every-smooth-quintic-threefold-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":52,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"6715066ebb74c262764fd200803a2c33a47351893e2b4d39a824c0fbe214f419","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-Gepner-stability-condition-on-every-smooth-quintic-threefold-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:ff8dbb92e7a55d2ef54c30b1cd6e1d893c252cf1802ef8922cbd5e326bf2acc0","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-Gepner-stability-condition-on-every-smooth-quintic-threefold-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L52"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nEvery smooth complex quintic threefold admits a numerical Bridgeland stability\ncondition $\\sigma=(Z,\\mathcal P)$ with the support property on $\\Knum(X)_{\\R}$\nsuch that, for every $E\\in\\D$ and $\\varphi\\in\\R$,\n\\[\n Z(\\Phi E)=e^{2\\pi i/5}Z(E),\\qquad\n \\Phi\\bigl(\\mathcal P(\\varphi)\\bigr)=\\mathcal P(\\varphi+2/5),\\qquad\n Z(\\OO_x)=-1\n\\]\nfor every closed point $x\\in X$."}
